  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have $\\int_0^2 f(x) d x=\\frac{3}{4} ;$ Now, $\\int_0^2 x f^{\\prime}(x) d x=x \\int_0^2 f^{\\prime}(x) d x-\\int_0^2 f(x) d x$\n$=[x f(x)]_0^2-\\frac{3}{4}=2 f(2)-\\frac{3}{4}=0-\\frac{3}{4}(\\because f(2)=0)=-\\frac{3}{4}$",
    "image": null
